                                    <watches>2</watches>
                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="14585423" author="corneadoug" created="Mon, 15 Jun 2015 04:49:52 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I found what the problem was.&lt;br/&gt;
Basically we set a dirtyText value when somebody type in the text editor, but we never release it when we run the query.&lt;br/&gt;
Checking the code, I am actually wondering if that value is really necessary.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The text editor value do not change, however the result do change based on what the other web browser run as query.&lt;br/&gt;
Even if it would be annoying to possibly change your text editor query while you type, it would be matching the query result.&lt;br/&gt;
And allow the user to get the other user query (otherwise it would override when he runs it)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Any feedback?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14585429" author="moon" created="Mon, 15 Jun 2015 04:57:38 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;It was designed to be update code (text editor content), when&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;  1. there is no local update&lt;br/&gt;
  2. and remote browser updated code and run paragraph&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Otherwise it is keeping it&apos;s content with dirty flag set.&lt;br/&gt;
but it looks like the feature has broken.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14585435" author="corneadoug" created="Mon, 15 Jun 2015 05:05:46 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Yes,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But this look weird in that case:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;User1 and User2 are on the same notebook and work on same paragraph.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;User1 change the query and run it&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;User2 Was changing the query too, he receives the new results and his text editor do not change&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;User2 can&apos;t get the updated query because its dirty, the only way would be to run his query, but in that case, it would update User1 result and text editor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</comment>
